2026-11-12T15:17:36.2933960Z """rl2_ppo_rollout -- CPU rollout / evaluation workers for rl2_ppo.
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2934434Z 
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2934844Z A worker task plays several FastCarbon games IN LOCKSTEP so the learner's
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2935594Z forward pass is batched over all their units (one NumPy call per step);
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2936328Z opponents are called per game. Game seeding follows eval_v53.play_game:
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2937021Z random.seed(rng_seed(seed, side)) -> sim.reset(seed) -> load opponent.
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2937786Z (With >1 lockstep game the global `random` stream is shared between the
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2938829Z games' opponents, so training games are not bit-reproducible vs play_game;
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2939542Z evaluation tasks therefore run one game per task.)
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2939956Z 
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2940213Z Opponent spec strings:
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2940763Z     "exp/opp_1cz_v5.py"      a bot file (module agent(), eval_v53 loader rule)
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2941629Z     "SNAP:<adapter>:<npz>"   frozen snapshot of a learner (greedy or sampled at
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2942377Z                              SNAP_TEMP), played through that adapter's actor
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2943673Z     "SNAP:cnet2:<npz>#T5"    any cnet2 policy net as a cheap fixed opponent (style row 5): no rule layer, no
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2944565Z                              search, trunk on the inference server -- costs what a snapshot costs
2026-11-12T15:17:36.2945209Z """
